   Let me first verify (d) empirically — run a quick scratch through the REAL runner instead of my broken node scratch. Actually simpler: add the test and see. Also — wait, I should double check the success path really removes agent:rework exactly once — removeConfiguredLabels normalizes ['agent:rework'] (dedupe) → one tracker.removeLabel call. Plus... `triggerConfiguredWorkflowForTicket` with stripKeys — not removal. `triggerSmIfIdle` — mocked. So yes, 1×.

